# Snake. Build it and run it in a terminal:
#
#     ./intent build examples/snake.intent && examples/snake
#
# Steer with the arrow keys; q stops. When the game is over, enter plays again.

The board is 30 wide and 14 high.

# Where the head is, and which way it is going.
The column starts at 10. The row starts at 7.
The sideways speed starts at 1. The downward speed starts at 0.

The length starts at 4.
The score starts at 0.
The food x starts at 20. The food y starts at 7.

# The body is the places the head has been lately.
Segments is a collection. Each segment has an x (number), a y (number) and an age (number).

# One step. Things that happen at the same moment happen in the order written.
Every 120 milliseconds, add a segment whose x is the column, whose y is the row and whose age is 0.
Every 120 milliseconds, the column increases by the sideways speed and the row increases by the downward speed.
Every 120 milliseconds, increase the age of every segment by 1.
Every 120 milliseconds, remove the segments whose age is at least the length.
Every 120 milliseconds, if the column is the food x and the row is the food y,
  the score increases by 1, the length increases by 1,
  the food x becomes a random number between 1 and 30,
  and the food y becomes a random number between 1 and 14.

# Steering. A snake cannot turn straight back on itself.
When the left key is pressed, if the sideways speed is 0, the sideways speed becomes -1 and the downward speed becomes 0.
When the right key is pressed, if the sideways speed is 0, the sideways speed becomes 1 and the downward speed becomes 0.
When the up key is pressed, if the downward speed is 0, the downward speed becomes -1 and the sideways speed becomes 0.
When the down key is pressed, if the downward speed is 0, the downward speed becomes 1 and the sideways speed becomes 0.

The game is over when the column is under 1 or the column is over 30 or the row is under 1 or the row is over 14.
The game is over when any segment's x is the column and its y is the row.

Draw each segment at its x and y as a green "o".
Draw a red "*" at the food x and the food y.
Draw a yellow "@" at the column and the row.
Show the score above the board.
